 ## Background
-Isometric Voxel Rendering is implemented in the Voxel2Pixel graphics library by Ben McLean [S1, unofficial]. It is designed for efficient rendering of voxel models in a fixed isometric projection, often used in games and visualization tools where a consistent, non-perspective view is preferred [S1, unofficial].
+Isometric Voxel Rendering is described in the Voxel2Pixel graphics library by Ben McLean [S1, unofficial]. The algorithm iterates over a 2D pixel grid to determine visible surfaces and uses a tiling system to draw triangles for exposed faces [S1, unofficial].
 
